<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toghon Taishi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1438</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toghon Taishi was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirats</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> in the early 15th century. Succeeding his father Bakhamu, he united the Oirat groups, defeated the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and in the 1430s became master of the steppe, ruling through a Chinggisid puppet khan, Toghtoa Bukha, since he could not take the title himself. His son Esen built on his power and captured the Ming emperor at Tumu in 1449.</p></div>
